croStrategy Tokenized stock (xStock)","price":92.16724778994451,"crypto_id":37215,"issuer_id":"6878977dcbbf471de3366e85","issuer_name":"Backed Assets","market_cap":261931.0273896973,"volume_24h":428175.67679185764},{"symbol":"MSTRc","name":"Strategy Inc. Tokenized Stock (Coinbase)","price":91.58397030380637,"crypto_id":42467,"issuer_id":"6a72fe7072996604d45c6733","issuer_name":"Coinbase","market_cap":2112107.5122389784,"volume_24h":19033883.83231775}],"tradfi_markets":[{"exchange":{"slug":"binance","name":"Binance","exchange_id":270},"ticker":"MSTR","market_url":"https://www.binance.com/en/stocks/EQ_MSTR"}]},"info":{"name":"MicroStrategy Inc","symbol":"MSTR","slug":"microstrategy","website":"https://www.strategy.com","employees":1483,"founded":"1989-01-01","industry":"Finance Services","cik":"0001050446","about":{"description":"### What is MicroStrategy Inc. (MSTR)?\n\nRetail investors seeking Bitcoin exposure via stock often hit roadblocks with ETFs or custody solutions. MicroStrategy solves that by packaging Bitcoin accumulation within a public equity wrapper.\n\nMicroStrategy-rebranded as Strategy™ in early 2025-is a Nasdaq-listed company specializing in business intelligence software while aggressively building Bitcoin reserves. It now identifies as a Bitcoin treasury company, using software revenue and capital markets to fund its crypto strategy.\n\n\n### Who is the CEO of MicroStrategy, and what is his role in the company’s Bitcoin strategy?\n\nInvestors often wonder who drives the strategy behind MSTR’s massive Bitcoin stash.\n\nMichael J. Saylor remains Executive Chairman and the chief architect of the Bitcoin treasury pivot. Phong Le, as President & CEO, handles operations. Saylor oversees capital raises and accumulation of BTC, while Le executes funding strategy and client-facing software services.\n\n\n### How does MicroStrategy generate revenue?\n\nTraditional software firms earn through software licensing and services-but with MSTR, Bitcoin rules the narrative.\n\nMicroStrategy continues to sell business intelligence software and mobile analytics tools under its legacy brand. On top of that, it leverages Bitcoin by issuing convertible notes, preferred shares, and equity to fund BTC purchases, expecting capital appreciation rather than cash income from crypto.\n\n\n### How has MSTR performed compared to Bitcoin since 2020?\n\nTraditional investors may not capture the full upside-MSTR often outperforms Bitcoin itself.\n\nFrom late 2020 to mid‑2025, MSTR stock surged roughly 3,558%, significantly exceeding Bitcoin’s 905% gain during the same period. While BTC appreciation drives the stock, MSTR’s leverage through debt and equity offerings amplifies returns-and volatility.\n\n\n### Could MicroStrategy tokenize its Bitcoin holdings or offer tokenized shares?\n\nMany expect tokenization from crypto-first firms. Strategy has already taken a bold step.\n\nMicroStrategy’s equity is offered as [tokenized stock] (https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/microstrategy-tokenized-stock-xstock/), such as MSTRX via xStocks and tokenized MSTR on Gemini (EU). That allows shares to trade on-chain, but BTC holdings themselves are not tokenized. Strategy hasn’t issued a stablecoin or Bitcoin-backed token-it tokenized its own equity only.\n\n\n### How does MicroStrategy plan to handle Bitcoin price volatility long-term?\n\nVolatility is a feature, not a bug, in Strategy’s model.\n\nWhile legacy software remains loss-making, Strategy uses capital tools (preferred shares, convertible notes) to fund BTC buys. It holds Bitcoin long-term, betting that appreciation outweighs risk. The company also retains flexibility to issue new equity or debt if needed, treating BTC as a long-duration asset.\n\n\n### How much Bitcoin does MicroStrategy own today?\n\nInvestors tracking BTC exposure need precise numbers-Strategy publishes updates regularly.\n\nAs of July 2025, Strategy holds 601,550 BTC, acquired at an average cost of ~$71,268 per coin, with a total cost basis near $42.9 billion. The holdings are valued at over $73 billion based on current price, representing about 3% of all Bitcoin in circulation.\n\n\n### Can you buy MicroStrategy tokenized shares on a blockchain?\n\nInvestors may look for equity tokens-yes, they exist for MSTR.\n\nTokenized versions such as MSTRX and FTX-based MSTR tokenized stock are available on platforms like xStocks and Gemini for EU users. These trade 24/7 and allow fractional ownership via stablecoins or crypto wallets.\n\n\n### What are the biggest risks of investing in MicroStrategy stock?\n\nInvesting in MSTR means not just equity risk, but crypto and financing risk.\n\nKey risks include Bitcoin price crashes, rising leverage costs, ESG and regulatory backlash, and software business underperformance. Token dilution from arrests of capital raises or preferred offerings may further pressure MSTR in bear markets.\n\n\n### Is MicroStrategy more of a Bitcoin ETF proxy or a traditional software company?\n\nIt began as software, but today it behaves more like a Bitcoin ETF proxy.\n\nWhile Strategy still sells BI software, its identity and valuation now derive primarily from Bitcoin holdings. Analysts view it as a leveraged, publicly traded proxy for BTC exposure-far removed from SaaS or mobile app revenue streams.","logo":null,"website":"https://www.strategy.com","date_added":"2025-07-17T07:28:04.000Z"},"rwa_id":114,"asset_type":"stock","rwa_rank":372,"has_tokens":true,"primary_exchange":"Nasdaq"},"tokenMeta":{"37003":{"id":37003,"name":"MicroStrategy tokenized stock (xStock)","symbol":"MSTRX","category":"token","description":"MicroStrategy tokenized stock (xStock) (MSTRX) is a cryptocurrency and operates on the Solana platform. MicroStrategy tokenized stock (xStock) has a current supply of 2,005,661.50655422 with 994,508.64848698 in circulation. The last known price of MicroStrategy tokenized stock (xStock) is 92.10297612 USD and is down -8.15 over the last 24 hours. It is currently 